# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Track generation scratch output
# random_trackgen.py writes here; generate_track_pool.py packages it into
# f1tenth_gym/maps/ and then deletes it. Ignored in case a run is interrupted.
/maps/

# Training output. Deliberately ignored in full, not just the checkpoints.
#
# A single 2M-step cell writes ~20 checkpoints plus their normalisation
# statistics, so the 8-cell grid produces several hundred binaries, and more
# once you add training seeds. They are also regenerable: pinning --seed and
# --track-seed exists precisely so a run can be reproduced from code rather
# than retrieved from git.
#
# Tracked model binaries have already caused trouble here. They appeared as
# opaque diffs in unrelated commits, and a merge came close to silently
# reverting them to older weights. If a final model needs archiving for the
# write-up, attach it to a release rather than committing it.
models/

# Evaluation figures are regenerated on every evaluate.py run.
generalization_results.png

# NOT ignored: results/
# Baseline reference numbers (random and gap-follower) are committed on
# purpose. They are fixed points the write-up cites, they are small CSVs, and
# they should be reviewable and diffable. They are only valid for the protocol
# that produced them, so regenerate them if the episode cap or the spawn line
# changes.

# OS and editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.claude/
*.swp
